<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monitorium of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1768</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Monitorium of Parma was a papal brief issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-xiii">Pope Clement XIII</a> on 30 January 1768 declaring null the church reforms of the Duchy of Parma, introduced by the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillaume-du-tillot">Guillaume du Tillot</a>, and threatening their authors with excommunication. Parma responded by expelling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>, and the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> courts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> backed the duke by seizing papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a>.</p></div>
